    requires_gpu: true
    max_turns: 50
    estimated_wall_time_min: 90
    gated_on:
      - experiment_id: exp952
        field: honest_verdict
        operator: eq
        value: "preflight_complete"
        rationale: "SOTA model must be pre-downloaded or experiment will time out before
                    writing a result file — same failure mode as Exp 942."
    prior_failures:
      - experiment_id: exp942-sota-math-repair-v2
        verdict: missing_result_file
        diagnosed_root_cause: "Experiment exited before writing result file; likely GGUF
          download timed out (30+ min for 20GB model). No error artifact written."
        addressed_by: "Exp 952 pre-downloads the model. Exp 953 adds a try/finally
          result-write guard: on any exception, write a partial artifact with
          status=blocked and stall_details before exit."
        retire_if_same_verdict: true
      - experiment_id: exp930-math-repair-e4b
        verdict: math_repair_zero
        diagnosed_root_cause: "gemma-4-E4B-it has 12% GSM8K baseline — no repair margin.
          Model capability ceiling confirmed."
        addressed_by: "Exp 953 uses Gemma4-31B (~75% GSM8K baseline) or Qwen3.6-35B
          (~80% baseline), pre-downloaded via Exp 952."
        retire_if_same_verdict: true
      - experiment_id: exp919-math-repair-gate-blocked
        verdict: blocked_gate_not_met
        diagnosed_root_cause: "Gate condition from prior SC-Energy experiment not met;
          gate was incorrectly applied to math repair."
        addressed_by: "Exp 953 has no SC-Energy gate — math repair is independent."
        retire_if_same_verdict: false
    description: |
      Run IterativeSelfRepair on 50 GSM8K math problems using Gemma4-31B-it GGUF
      (or Qwen3.6-35B-A3B if Gemma4-31B not ready). MANDATORY structure:
        try:
          [experiment code]
          write success artifact
        except Exception as e:
          write partial artifact with status=blocked, stall_details=str(e)
          raise
      This ensures a result file always exists regardless of exit mode.
      Primary metric: pass@1 accuracy before vs after repair (should be >0 delta
      for SOTA model vs 0.0 for E4B). Secondary: number of successful repairs / total.
      If delta=0 again with SOTA model: write honest_verdict=sota_ceiling_confirmed
      and retire the entire math-repair-iterative-self-repair experiment line.
      Use MODEL_SPECS with unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF as primary, unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF
      as fallback. Pre-warm GPU via tmpl.setup_gpu(MODEL_SPECS) before timed inference.
    result_schema:
      honest_verdict: str
      baseline_accuracy: float
      repair_accuracy: float
      repair_delta: float
      n_problems: int
      model_used: str

  - id: exp954
    title: "Fast-Path Probe Live GPU Validation — SpilledEnergy + ThinkPRM + DRIFTProbe"
    priority: high
    requires_gpu: true
    max_turns: 30
    estimated_wall_time_min: 60
    gated_on:
      - experiment_id: exp949
        field: honest_verdict
        operator: in
        value: ["spilled_energy_viable"]
        rationale: "SpilledEnergy CPU result must be established before GPU validation."
      - experiment_id: exp945
        field: honest_verdict
        operator: in
        value: ["thinkprm_viable"]
        rationale: "ThinkPRM CPU result must be established before GPU validation."
      - experiment_id: exp947
        field: honest_verdict
        operator: in
        value: ["depth_recurrent_improves", "depth_recurrent_marginal"]
        rationale: "DRIFTProbe v3 CPU result must be established before GPU validation."
    description: |
      Validate three CPU-proven probes against real live Gemma4-31B responses on the ROCm GPU.
      CLAUSE.md mandate: "All headline results must have live GPU provenance."
      Exp 949 (SpilledEnergy AUROC=1.0), Exp 945 (ThinkPRM AUROC=0.99), Exp 947
      (DRIFTProbe v3 probe_auc=0.5807) — all CPU only.
      Protocol:
        1. Load Gemma4-31B-it-GGUF on ROCm GPU (sg render -c '...')
        2. Generate 100 real responses to factual questions with deliberate errors injected
        3. Run SpilledEnergy (logit chain-rule energy) on these real responses
        4. Run ThinkPRM CoT verification step on these real responses
        5. Run DRIFTProbe v3 (depth-recurrent attention pooling) on these real responses
        6. Compute AUROC for each probe vs ground-truth error labels
      Acceptance thresholds (from Gap 2 analysis):
        - SpilledEnergy AUROC >= 0.80 (degradation from 1.0 expected on real data)
        - ThinkPRM AUROC >= 0.85 (degradation from 0.99 expected on real data)
        - DRIFTProbe AUROC >= 0.55 (marginal acceptable given 0.5807 CPU baseline)
      Use unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF. Pre-warm via tmpl.setup_gpu(MODEL_SPECS).
    result_schema:
      honest_verdict: str
      spilled_energy_auroc: float
      thinkprm_auroc: float
      driftprobe_auroc: float
      n_responses: int
      model_used: str

  - id: exp955
    title: "Triple Integration — SC-Energy + SpilledEnergy + ThinkPRM into ThreeTierPipeline"
    priority: high
    requires_gpu: false
    max_turns: 50
    estimated_wall_time_min: 60
    gated_on:
      - experiment_id: exp944
        field: honest_verdict
        operator: in
        value: ["sc_energy_viable"]
        rationale: "SC-Energy must be CPU-validated before pipeline integration."
    description: |
      Wire three validated probes into ThreeTierPipeline as production Tier components:
        - SpilledEnergy (arXiv 2602.18671) as Tier 0 fast reject (training-free, logit-based)
        - ThinkPRM (arXiv 2504.16828) as Tier 2.9 CoT step verifier (generative, slow)
        - SC-Energy (arXiv 2503.10695) as Tier 3 set-level consistency energy (EBM-based)
      Integration architecture:
        Tier 0 (SpilledEnergy) → fast, runs on every response, rejects obvious errors
        Tier 2.9 (ThinkPRM) → medium, runs when Tier 0 uncertain, verifies reasoning steps
        Tier 3 (SC-Energy) → slow, runs when Tier 2.9 uncertain, energy-based set consistency
      Required: end-to-end integration test with synthetic input showing all three tiers
      activate in cascade. Write artifacts at results/experiment_955_triple_integration.json.
      honest_verdict should be "triple_integration_viable" if all three tiers wire without
      import errors and the cascade test passes.
    result_schema:
      honest_verdict: str
      tier0_wired: bool
      tier29_wired: bool
      tier3_wired: bool
      cascade_test_passed: bool

  - id: exp956
    title: "DualGPU VerifyRepairPipeline Wiring — Production Integration"
    priority: high
    requires_gpu: true
    max_turns: 50
    estimated_wall_time_min: 90
    prior_failures:
      - experiment_id: exp932-dualgpu-benchmark
        verdict: dualgpu_benchmark_valid
        diagnosed_root_cause: "Exp 932 benchmarked DualGPU at 1.96x throughput on realistic
          workload (Milestone .72) but only as a standalone benchmark, never wired into
          VerifyRepairPipeline. 8 consecutive milestones of idle deployment."
        addressed_by: "Exp 956 specifically targets production wiring, not benchmarking.
          Success criterion is VerifyRepairPipeline using DualGPURunner by default when
          two GPUs are detected, with verified throughput >= 1.5x vs single GPU."
        retire_if_same_verdict: false
    description: |
      Wire DualGPURunner (already benchmarked at 1.96x in Exp 932) into VerifyRepairPipeline
      as the default execution path when two GPUs are detected.
      Implementation:
        1. Read the existing DualGPURunner implementation from Exp 932
        2. Add GPU detection to VerifyRepairPipeline.__init__:
           if torch.cuda.device_count() >= 2: self.runner = DualGPURunner()
           else: self.runner = SingleGPURunner()
        3. Add integration test: run pipeline on 20 real inputs with 2-GPU configuration,
           verify throughput >= 1.5x vs single GPU baseline
        4. Add docstring explaining WHY: "DualGPU is used when available because Exp 932
           showed 1.96x throughput at realistic batch sizes; the single-GPU path is
           preserved for machines with one GPU or when debugging."
      If throughput in production pipeline is NOT >= 1.5x:
        - Write honest_verdict=dualgpu_wired_below_target with measured_speedup
        - Do NOT re-propose DualGPU optimization — retire the optimization track
      MANDATORY: add Exp 641 (which is the DualGPU gate cascade blocker) to exclusion
      manifest entry noting that Exp 956 production wiring closes the underlying gap.
    result_schema:
      honest_verdict: str
      measured_speedup: float
      pipeline_wired: bool
      integration_test_passed: bool

  - id: exp957
    title: "FR-11 JEPA v23 — SC-Energy Coherence Labels as Training Signal"
    priority: medium
    requires_gpu: false
    max_turns: 50
    estimated_wall_time_min: 120
    gated_on:
      - experiment_id: exp944
        field: honest_verdict
        operator: in
        value: ["sc_energy_viable"]
        rationale: "SC-Energy must produce reliable coherence scores to serve as
                    training labels for JEPA. If SC-Energy is not viable, the
                    coherence labels are noise — JEPA training would not converge."
    prior_failures:
      - experiment_id: exp-jepa-v17-through-v22
        verdict: jepa_ood_below_target
        diagnosed_root_cause: "Self-supervised forward-world-model loss provides
          insufficient gradient signal to separate in-distribution from OOD.
          The model learns to predict future states well but does not learn a
          discriminative boundary between valid and invalid reasoning chains."
        addressed_by: "JEPA v23 adds SC-Energy coherence scores (AUROC=0.9017, Exp 944)
          as auxiliary training supervision. This provides direct gradient signal toward
          the OOD detection objective: low SC-Energy coherence = likely OOD. The auxiliary
          loss is weighted at 0.3 (primary: 0.7 forward-model loss) to preserve the
          world-model structure while shaping the latent space."
        retire_if_same_verdict: true
    description: |
      FR-11 (autonomous self-learning loop) JEPA has stalled below OOD AUC=0.75 across
      v17-v22 (6 consecutive milestones). Root cause: self-supervised loss lacks
      discriminative gradient toward OOD boundary.
      JEPA v23 approach:
        1. Load JEPA v22 checkpoint as starting point
        2. Compute SC-Energy coherence scores for training examples (from Exp 944 model)
        3. Add auxiliary classification loss: predict SC-Energy coherence bucket (high/low)
           from JEPA latent representation. Loss weight: 0.3 (auxiliary) / 0.7 (world model)
        4. Train for 50 epochs on JAX with CPU
        5. Evaluate OOD AUC on held-out set (same protocol as v17-v22)
      If OOD AUC > 0.75: honest_verdict = jepa_v23_ood_viable. Close FR-11 RETRO.
      If OOD AUC <= 0.75 (same verdict as v17-v22): honest_verdict = jepa_retired.
        Add JEPA-v17-v22-all-ooe-below-target to exclusion manifest.
        Write FR-11 status: "JEPA approach to OOD detection not viable after 7 attempts.
        Alternative: use SC-Energy directly as the OOD detector (AUROC=0.9017)."
      Use JAX_PLATFORMS=cpu for reproducibility (per CLAUDE.md).
    result_schema:
      honest_verdict: str
      ood_auc: float
      auxiliary_loss_weight: float
      epochs_trained: int

  - id: exp958
    title: "KV260 v4 RTL — Sparse E-MVL Ising Sampler Implementation"
    priority: medium
    requires_gpu: false
    max_turns: 50
    estimated_wall_time_min: 120
    gated_on:
      - experiment_id: exp950
        field: honest_verdict
        operator: in
        value: ["emvl_comparable"]
        rationale: "v4 RTL spec was written in Exp 950. Implementation must follow
                    the spec at hardware/kv260/ising_sampler_v4_spec.md."
    prior_failures:
      - experiment_id: exp950-emvl-sparsified-ising
        verdict: emvl_comparable
        diagnosed_root_cause: "Exp 950 wrote the v4 RTL spec but did not implement RTL.
          Result was spec + software simulation only. No VHDL/Verilog was written."
        addressed_by: "Exp 958 implements the RTL per the written spec. OSS-CAD-Suite
          is confirmed installed (from research-hardware-wishlist.md). KV260 board arrived
          2026-04-20. This is the first implementation attempt after spec was written."
        retire_if_same_verdict: false
      - experiment_id: exp585-kv260-bitfile-blocked
        verdict: blocked_no_bitfile
        diagnosed_root_cause: "Vivado not available; could not generate bitfile."
        addressed_by: "Exp 958 uses OSS-CAD-Suite (yosys + nextpnr-xilinx) instead of
          Vivado. Target: synthesizable RTL + yosys synthesis passing, NOT full bitfile.
          Bitfile generation deferred to Exp 959+."
        retire_if_same_verdict: false
      - experiment_id: exp624-ising-simulation-only
        verdict: simulation_only
        diagnosed_root_cause: "RTL simulation passed but no synthesis target."
        addressed_by: "Exp 958 targets yosys synthesis with LUT count verification
          against the 36,250 LUT estimate from Exp 950 (within KV260 117K budget)."
        retire_if_same_verdict: false
    description: |
      Implement the Sparse E-MVL Ising Sampler v4 in synthesizable VHDL or Verilog
      following the spec at hardware/kv260/ising_sampler_v4_spec.md.
      Implementation steps:
        1. Read the v4 spec entirely before writing any RTL
        2. Implement the sparse coupling matrix (K=16 nonzero couplings per spin, N=128)
           using block RAM with address-indexed coupling lists
        3. Implement the Metropolis-Hastings acceptance logic in RTL
        4. Implement the random number generator (LFSR-based per spec)
        5. Run yosys synthesis: yosys -p "synth_xilinx -flatten -top ising_sampler_v4" design.v
        6. Verify LUT count is within 36,250 estimate (+/- 20% tolerance)
        7. Run iverilog simulation with testbench verifying basic Ising distribution shape
      honest_verdict options:
        "rtl_synthesizes_within_budget" — yosys passes, LUT count <= 43,500 (36,250 * 1.2)
        "rtl_synthesizes_over_budget" — yosys passes but LUT count exceeds budget
        "rtl_synthesis_fails" — yosys reports errors
        "rtl_not_written" — implementation did not complete (write with stall_details)
      Use OSS-CAD-Suite tools available via PATH after installation at research-hardware-wishlist.md.
    result_schema:
      honest_verdict: str
      lut_count: int
      lut_budget: int
      yosys_passes: bool
      simulation_passes: bool

  - id: exp959
    title: "IterativeSelfRepair 100q Scale-Up + DebugRepair Hypothesis Step"
    priority: medium
    requires_gpu: true
    max_turns: 50
    estimated_wall_time_min: 120
    gated_on:
      - experiment_id: exp952
        field: honest_verdict
        operator: in
        value: ["preflight_complete"]
        rationale: "SOTA model must be pre-downloaded. Exp 906 burned 30+ min on SOTA
                    download within timed GPU experiment; cannot repeat."
    prior_failures:
      - experiment_id: exp906-iterative-repair-slow-sota-download
        verdict: slow_sota_download
        diagnosed_root_cause: "SOTA model was not pre-cached; download took 30+ min
          during timed experiment, eating into wall time budget."
        addressed_by: "Exp 952 pre-downloads all SOTA models. Exp 959 gates on
          exp952 confirming soma_models_ready=true."
        retire_if_same_verdict: false
      - experiment_id: exp905-iterative-repair-25q-baseline
        verdict: repair_viable
        diagnosed_root_cause: "25q scale-up only; no DebugRepair hypothesis step.
          Not a failure — Exp 959 extends to 100q and adds DebugRepair."
        addressed_by: "Exp 959 scales to 100q (4x scale-up) and adds DebugRepair
          hypothesis step from arXiv 2604.19305 (+8.2pp HumanEval vs standard repair)."
        retire_if_same_verdict: false
    description: |
      Scale IterativeSelfRepair from 25q (Exp 905) to 100q AND add the DebugRepair
      hypothesis step from arXiv 2604.19305.
      DebugRepair hypothesis step: before generating a repair, generate a hypothesis
      about WHY the initial response is wrong. The hypothesis is fed into the repair
      prompt as context: "My diagnosis of the error: {hypothesis}. Now generate a
      corrected response." arXiv 2604.19305 reports +8.2pp HumanEval with this step.
      MODEL_SPECS:
        primary: unsloth/gemma-4-31B-it-GGUF
        fallback: unsloth/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-GGUF
      Domains: code (100 HumanEval problems) + math (50 GSM8K problems).
      Metrics:
        - code_pass_at_1_before, code_pass_at_1_after, code_repair_delta
        - math_pass_at_1_before, math_pass_at_1_after, math_repair_delta
        - hypothesis_contribution: AUC(with_hypothesis) - AUC(without_hypothesis)
      Use BatchedInferenceRunner with batch_size=8. Pre-warm GPU via tmpl.setup_gpu().
      honest_verdict = "iterative_repair_100q_viable" if either domain shows delta > 0.
    result_schema:
      honest_verdict: str
      code_repair_delta: float
      math_repair_delta: float
      hypothesis_contribution: float
      n_problems_code: int
      n_problems_math: int
      model_used: str

  - id: exp960
    title: "Symbolic-KAN v2 Pipeline Deploy + HuggingFace Publish"
    priority: medium
    requires_gpu: false
    max_turns: 30
    estimated_wall_time_min: 45
    gated_on:
      - experiment_id: exp948
        field: honest_verdict
        operator: in
        value: ["symbolic_kan_real_viable"]
        rationale: "Symbolic-KAN AUC=1.0 on real FoVer data (Exp 948) must be confirmed
                    before deploying to production. Cannot deploy a model that has not
                    proven its discriminative capability on real data."
    prior_failures:
      - experiment_id: exp937-symbolic-kan-synthetic
        verdict: symbolic_kan_synthetic_viable
        diagnosed_root_cause: "Exp 937 validated Symbolic-KAN on SYNTHETIC arithmetic
          violations only (AUC=0.9344). Not a failure per se; Exp 948 was the planned
          real-data follow-up."
        addressed_by: "Exp 948 confirmed AUC=1.0 on 57 real FoVer pairs. Exp 960
          deploys this proven model."
        retire_if_same_verdict: false
    description: |
      Deploy the Symbolic-KAN model (proven at AUC=1.0 in Exp 948) to:
        (a) Production ThreeTierPipeline as the default Tier 3 verifier
        (b) HuggingFace Hub at huggingface.co/Carnot-EBM with model card
        (c) IPFS mirror (dual-distribution per CLAUDE.md rule 3)
      Implementation steps:
        1. Load the Symbolic-KAN checkpoint from Exp 948 results
        2. Register it as a Tier 3 verifier in ThreeTierPipeline
        3. Write a brief integration test: 5 real FoVer examples, AUC must be >= 0.90
        4. Push model + config + README to huggingface.co/Carnot-EBM/symbolic-kan-v2
           using huggingface_hub Python client
        5. Pin to IPFS: ipfs add -r symbolic_kan_v2_model/
        6. Record IPFS CID in model card and in ops/changelog.md
      Model card must be emoji-free (per CLAUDE.md no-emoji rule) and include:
        - AUC=1.0 on 57 real FoVer pairs provenance (Exp 948)
        - Training set size and violation types
        - Intended use: Carnot ThreeTierPipeline Tier 3 verifier
        - Limitations: validated on FoVer violation types only; may not generalize
      honest_verdict = "symbolic_kan_deployed" if HF push succeeds and integration test passes.
    result_schema:
      honest_verdict: str
      hf_repo_url: str
      ipfs_cid: str
      integration_test_auc: float
      pipeline_registered: bool

